WEBVTT

00:00:02.390 --> 00:00:06.150
Planning Proposal for After Party

00:00:17.080 --> 00:00:18.160
No, no.

00:02:13.980 --> 00:02:16.920
<b>Quest 08     Turning Point</b>

00:02:18.370 --> 00:02:20.160
Morning-daisy, Ai-Ai!

00:02:20.160 --> 00:02:21.470
Good morning!

00:02:21.470 --> 00:02:22.600
Good morning!

00:02:23.340 --> 00:02:24.350
Good morning.

00:02:36.510 --> 00:02:39.310
Let's discuss the details after school.

00:02:39.310 --> 00:02:40.380
Got it.

00:02:40.380 --> 00:02:41.760
Good work, everyone.

00:02:41.760 --> 00:02:43.140
Good work.

00:02:47.880 --> 00:02:51.900
Will the club presidents 
agree to this proposal?

00:02:52.330 --> 00:02:57.720
I think they will once they see we're willing
to handle all miscellaneous tasks.

00:02:58.060 --> 00:03:03.160
What matters now is how little we 
can make them think we compromised.

00:03:04.330 --> 00:03:07.290
You mean, so they don't think 
we're being condescending?

00:03:07.290 --> 00:03:08.280
Yes.

00:03:11.390 --> 00:03:12.980
Now, if you'll excuse me.

00:03:15.260 --> 00:03:17.520
How we tell them, huh?

00:03:25.750 --> 00:03:28.700
You're still thinking about 
the other day's quest?

00:03:28.700 --> 00:03:31.820
I told you about Konoe-san's cut.

00:03:32.120 --> 00:03:33.260
It's a coincidence.

00:03:33.260 --> 00:03:35.310
Even if is, I can't stop thinking about it.

00:03:35.310 --> 00:03:37.920
Suzuki-san must be hiding something.

00:03:38.970 --> 00:03:42.840
Playing detective is all well and good,
but I need you to work on the after party.

00:03:42.840 --> 00:03:46.780
But you're the one who suggested
we hold an after party in the first place.

00:03:50.060 --> 00:03:51.420
I'm counting on you.

00:03:56.260 --> 00:03:58.670
Izumi-senpai, good morning.

00:03:58.670 --> 00:03:59.960
Good morning.

00:03:59.960 --> 00:04:01.070
Good morning.

00:04:01.430 --> 00:04:02.420
Good morning.

00:04:02.420 --> 00:04:03.470
Good morning.

00:04:03.470 --> 00:04:05.900
Izumi-senpai sure is great.

00:04:05.900 --> 00:04:07.470
I admire her.

00:04:07.470 --> 00:04:09.590
During a certain emperor's reign,

00:04:09.590 --> 00:04:13.000
while a number of court ladies and 
attendants were serving him,

00:04:13.000 --> 00:04:15.800
there was one lady of not 
particularly noble status

00:04:15.800 --> 00:04:17.730
who had earned his favor...

00:04:41.340 --> 00:04:42.760
Can I help you?

00:04:44.920 --> 00:04:48.760
Looks like you're headed 
somewhere deserted for lunch.

00:04:49.120 --> 00:04:50.370
I'm going to the PE storeroom.

00:04:50.660 --> 00:04:52.770
I was asked to set up for PE this afternoon.

00:04:53.600 --> 00:04:55.460
Oh, really?

00:04:55.760 --> 00:04:57.650
Have you taken an interest in me?

00:04:57.650 --> 00:04:58.270
What?

00:05:01.070 --> 00:05:02.920
Yeah, pretty interested.

00:05:02.920 --> 00:05:04.180
Is he confessing?

00:05:04.180 --> 00:05:06.030
No, he's responding to her confession...

00:05:07.380 --> 00:05:08.200
...of love.

00:05:08.600 --> 00:05:11.230
Oh, no. It's not like that.

00:05:11.230 --> 00:05:12.400
Really.

00:05:12.400 --> 00:05:13.240
Excuses.

00:05:13.240 --> 00:05:14.270
Unseemly.

00:05:14.270 --> 00:05:15.710
Say something!

00:05:16.610 --> 00:05:17.960
What do you want me to say?

00:05:17.960 --> 00:05:19.500
What? Well...

00:05:19.500 --> 00:05:21.410
Hey, hold on.

00:05:21.730 --> 00:05:22.720
Rejected?

00:05:22.720 --> 00:05:23.920
Rejected.

00:05:23.920 --> 00:05:26.470
You guys are even more 
in sync than usual today.

00:05:26.980 --> 00:05:28.040
Anyway,

00:05:28.040 --> 00:05:32.190
I thought of a way to distribute 
the after party proposal.

00:05:32.190 --> 00:05:33.220
Dodging the issue.

00:05:33.840 --> 00:05:35.800
<i>Give me a break...</i>

00:05:38.620 --> 00:05:42.700
So the student council will 
manage and execute everything.

00:05:43.000 --> 00:05:45.220
Please. At least consider it.

00:05:45.500 --> 00:05:49.030
Captain, Itsuki helps us out all the time.

00:05:49.030 --> 00:05:50.960
Yeah, but...

00:05:50.960 --> 00:05:52.240
Please.

00:05:53.100 --> 00:05:56.040
What? Oh, no. President, please...

00:05:56.040 --> 00:05:58.170
Do we have your support, then?

00:06:00.130 --> 00:06:02.670
In that case, well...

00:06:02.670 --> 00:06:05.000
I'll talk to the manager

00:06:05.620 --> 00:06:06.670
and try to be positive...

00:06:06.670 --> 00:06:08.250
Thank you.

00:06:11.400 --> 00:06:12.320
Please.

00:06:12.320 --> 00:06:13.680
No, thank you.

00:06:18.940 --> 00:06:19.560
Planning Proposal for After Party

00:06:33.080 --> 00:06:34.450
Thank you.

00:06:40.560 --> 00:06:43.830
Will doing this over and 
over again really work?

00:06:43.830 --> 00:06:45.880
Things seem to be going well so far.

00:06:46.400 --> 00:06:49.800
You're popular to begin with,

00:06:49.800 --> 00:06:51.630
so people will listen if you talk to them.

00:06:51.630 --> 00:06:53.140
Hey, hold on a minute!

00:06:53.140 --> 00:06:54.230
Kota?

00:06:54.230 --> 00:06:57.720
I heard Rina-senpai's going around 
convincing all the club presidents!

00:06:57.720 --> 00:06:58.640
Yeah.

00:06:58.960 --> 00:07:02.150
And on top of her clasping her 
hands with tears in her eyes

00:07:02.150 --> 00:07:07.920
and begging please, she'll do anything?

00:07:07.920 --> 00:07:09.650
Who told you that?

00:07:10.000 --> 00:07:11.960
Why haven't you come to the karate club?

00:07:11.960 --> 00:07:14.540
Weren't you in favor all along?

00:07:14.860 --> 00:07:17.160
Maybe I'll switch sides, then.

00:07:17.660 --> 00:07:18.910
Kota-kun.

00:07:19.660 --> 00:07:22.900
Pre-tty puh-leeze!

00:07:22.900 --> 00:07:24.060
That's creepy.

00:07:25.000 --> 00:07:27.140
Man, you sure are acting funny.

00:07:27.140 --> 00:07:30.670
Is it because you confessed 
your feelings for Aika-chan?

00:07:30.670 --> 00:07:31.480
What?

00:07:31.480 --> 00:07:32.580
You did?

00:07:32.580 --> 00:07:33.540
No!

00:07:33.540 --> 00:07:34.930
Apparently he did.

00:07:34.930 --> 00:07:39.860
The two of them should just emcee
the after party together already.

00:07:39.860 --> 00:07:41.030
We're not going to!

00:07:41.960 --> 00:07:44.280
It's not like that. I told you this morning.

00:07:44.280 --> 00:07:45.120
Suzuki-san is—

00:07:45.120 --> 00:07:46.270
Why don't you, then?

00:07:46.270 --> 00:07:46.940
What?

00:07:47.390 --> 00:07:49.570
Emcee the event with Aika-san.

00:07:51.420 --> 00:07:53.160
I'm not going to do that.

00:07:53.160 --> 00:07:54.990
What's going on?

00:07:55.240 --> 00:07:56.990
Pockets on both sides

00:07:55.240 --> 00:07:56.990
Tights

00:07:55.410 --> 00:07:56.990
<b>Maid Uniform</b>

00:07:55.530 --> 00:07:56.990
Wrists
Frills and ribbons
Make it cute <3

00:07:55.660 --> 00:07:56.990
Ribbon hemmed with thin lace

00:07:57.390 --> 00:07:58.380
Wait on customers?

00:07:58.380 --> 00:08:00.500
Yeah, at the maid café our class is holding.

00:08:01.110 --> 00:08:03.920
Ai-Ai, will you wait on customers with us?

00:08:03.920 --> 00:08:05.380
You've got a nice body.

00:08:05.380 --> 00:08:07.260
I know you'd look great in the uniform.

00:08:07.260 --> 00:08:09.330
It would definitely be a huge success.

00:08:10.040 --> 00:08:12.780
Do I need this ribbon to wait on customers?

00:08:11.380 --> 00:08:15.390
Ribbon on the back
Lace edges

00:08:12.780 --> 00:08:14.310
The ribbon is important.

00:08:14.310 --> 00:08:15.390
Huh...

00:08:16.230 --> 00:08:17.390
You won't?

00:08:17.820 --> 00:08:18.920
I don't mind.

00:08:18.920 --> 00:08:20.140
Really?

00:08:20.140 --> 00:08:24.510
As a member of this class, 
assisting you is one of my responsibilities.

00:08:24.510 --> 00:08:26.150
Thanks, Ai-Ai!

00:08:27.470 --> 00:08:29.150
That's great.

00:08:31.320 --> 00:08:32.900
Excuse us.

00:08:35.420 --> 00:08:39.200
If we can get approval from all the 
club presidents and class reps,

00:08:39.200 --> 00:08:40.420
we'll be good to go.

00:08:43.280 --> 00:08:44.410
Do you want to do it that badly?

00:08:46.660 --> 00:08:48.170
Emcee for the after party.

00:08:49.900 --> 00:08:51.170
I told you...

00:08:51.800 --> 00:08:55.180
You're the one who suggested
an after party in the first place.

00:08:55.510 --> 00:08:57.540
Someone disappeared again?

00:08:57.860 --> 00:09:01.610
<i>They've become more active lately.</i>

00:09:01.610 --> 00:09:02.740
I understand.

00:09:03.010 --> 00:09:05.470
I'll collect information tomorrow.

00:09:05.470 --> 00:09:07.190
<i>The situation has become quite tense.</i>

00:09:07.820 --> 00:09:09.830
<i>I shouldn't need to emphasize this, but...</i>

00:09:09.830 --> 00:09:10.690
What?

00:09:11.120 --> 00:09:15.680
<i>Don't forget that you're there on a mission.</i>

00:09:16.760 --> 00:09:17.360
Yes, sir.

00:09:22.370 --> 00:09:24.120
<b>Maid Uniform</b>

00:09:28.380 --> 00:09:32.960
<b>[Dragonkin]</b> Creatures that inhabit Planet Amduscia. While they may have individually distinct appearances, they're all part of the same species. Aggressive by nature, but Darker corruption makes them go berserk and attack ARKS as enemies. Most notable among them is the Vole Dragon, which has traumatized several ARKS as the first formidable enemy they face.

00:09:32.960 --> 00:09:37.550
<b>[Ether]</b> A particle discovered in 2016, it largely remains a mystery in 2026. With the ability to transfer data at extremely high speeds, it changed the world as people knew it. The ESC-A towers constructed all over the world disseminate Ether, making high-speed, wireless communication possible.

00:09:38.680 --> 00:09:41.200
She's a blonde summoner.

00:09:41.720 --> 00:09:43.560
A summoner, huh?

00:09:43.560 --> 00:09:45.560
I don't know.

00:09:46.220 --> 00:09:47.620
Did something happen?

00:09:47.950 --> 00:09:48.810
Oh, good.

00:09:49.370 --> 00:09:50.760
Will you help me?

00:09:50.760 --> 00:09:54.360
I'm asking around to see if anyone's 
seen Suzuki-san in game.

00:09:55.740 --> 00:09:56.840
Is there a problem?

00:09:57.140 --> 00:10:01.020
I see you're quite infatuated with her
both in real life and at Oracle.

00:10:03.250 --> 00:10:04.080
What?

00:10:04.080 --> 00:10:06.090
Are you mad about something?

00:10:06.400 --> 00:10:07.430
Not really.

00:10:07.860 --> 00:10:10.250
Kid! Silver!

00:10:13.460 --> 00:10:14.640
Aika?

00:10:14.640 --> 00:10:16.340
She's a blonde summoner

00:10:16.800 --> 00:10:19.460
who wears a beret and a ribbon on her chest.

00:10:19.770 --> 00:10:21.550
You've been observing her quite closely.

00:10:22.700 --> 00:10:25.900
There are a lot of ARKS who look like that.

00:10:25.900 --> 00:10:28.020
Let me know if you see her.

00:10:29.100 --> 00:10:29.800
Hey.

00:10:30.280 --> 00:10:34.870
How long did it take for that person 
who went missing to come back?

00:10:34.870 --> 00:10:35.610
What?

00:10:35.610 --> 00:10:37.260
You mean Konoe-san?

00:10:37.580 --> 00:10:38.290
Yeah.

00:10:38.290 --> 00:10:41.620
She came back two days later.
Why do you ask?

00:10:45.240 --> 00:10:48.580
A college student went missing
in her neighborhood.

00:10:49.440 --> 00:10:51.580
It's been happening a lot lately, right?

00:10:54.070 --> 00:11:01.340
And apparently some staff went missing at the
ARKS Fan Festa that was held the other day.

00:11:01.340 --> 00:11:04.570
Silver, what does this missing person look like?

00:11:04.890 --> 00:11:06.200
Why are you asking?

00:11:06.480 --> 00:11:08.610
They could be in a field somewhere.

00:11:08.610 --> 00:11:11.350
That's impossible. We're talking about
a real-life human here.

00:11:11.350 --> 00:11:15.310
You still think Mika was actually here?

00:11:15.560 --> 00:11:17.860
If we find the missing college student,

00:11:17.860 --> 00:11:20.640
Suzuki-san might appear there again.

00:11:20.980 --> 00:11:21.960
Let's look for them.

00:11:22.240 --> 00:11:23.620
Look for them yourself.

00:11:23.620 --> 00:11:24.480
What?

00:11:24.820 --> 00:11:26.120
<i>Emergency alert.</i>

00:11:26.440 --> 00:11:30.080
<i>The ARKS Ship City is 
under attack by Darkers.</i>

00:11:30.180 --> 00:11:32.750
Hey, wait! Wait up!

00:11:30.400 --> 00:11:33.630
<i>All ARKS please report to the 
nearest quest counter immediately.</i>

00:11:42.940 --> 00:11:44.390
Itsuki-kun!

00:11:44.970 --> 00:11:49.260
That limited edition rare item 
you were after is on Game Mate—

00:11:52.360 --> 00:11:54.980
Don't we have a meeting with the president?

00:12:32.480 --> 00:12:34.980
Tailing someone is meaningless
if you do it that poorly.

00:12:37.640 --> 00:12:39.260
You didn't notice me until now.

00:12:39.260 --> 00:12:40.890
I noticed you from the start.

00:12:41.230 --> 00:12:44.530
You were so obvious, I didn't even 
feel like trying to lose you.

00:12:44.890 --> 00:12:48.740
If you're curious, instead of 
sneaking around, come at me openly.

00:12:51.700 --> 00:12:53.580
What are you doing all the way out here?

00:12:53.880 --> 00:12:55.710
I don't have to tell you that.

00:12:56.950 --> 00:13:01.600
<i>This massive tower, tall enough to 
pierce the heavens, is the ESC-A Tower.</i>

00:13:02.140 --> 00:13:06.640
<i>Along with the popularization of 
high-speed wireless communications</i>

00:13:04.060 --> 00:13:06.640
I've never seen it up close before.

00:13:06.640 --> 00:13:11.390
<i>known as "Ether Communications" 
and an international commitment,</i>

00:13:07.120 --> 00:13:09.690
It's bigger than I imagined.

00:13:11.390 --> 00:13:14.640
<i>construction of said towers 
began across the world in 2016.</i>

00:13:15.010 --> 00:13:16.480
"Keep out"...

00:13:16.480 --> 00:13:17.770
Itsuki?

00:13:18.100 --> 00:13:19.130
Silver.

00:13:19.610 --> 00:13:21.780
On a date? Way to go.

00:13:21.780 --> 00:13:23.780
Actually, no.

00:13:24.090 --> 00:13:25.930
What are you doing here?

00:13:25.930 --> 00:13:28.030
My house is nearby.

00:13:28.030 --> 00:13:30.140
What? Oh, really?

00:13:31.200 --> 00:13:33.040
Is that where you're headed?

00:13:33.500 --> 00:13:36.820
It's a popular place, with cafés and stuff.

00:13:36.820 --> 00:13:38.160
It's too bad, though.

00:13:38.540 --> 00:13:39.940
Did something happen?

00:13:40.220 --> 00:13:44.360
Remember the missing college 
student I told you about?

00:13:44.710 --> 00:13:46.550
They disappeared inside there.

00:13:49.600 --> 00:13:52.400
Is that where you were headed?

00:13:52.400 --> 00:13:55.240
Is that any way to talk to her?

00:13:55.690 --> 00:13:57.120
Hey, wait!

00:13:57.120 --> 00:13:59.100
Look. You made her mad.

00:13:59.100 --> 00:14:00.410
It's not like that.

00:14:00.410 --> 00:14:03.900
Fine, then. Want me to go 
on a date with you instead?

00:14:04.310 --> 00:14:05.400
What?

00:14:05.400 --> 00:14:07.310
I want ice cream!

00:14:07.310 --> 00:14:08.910
Hey, wait!

00:14:12.190 --> 00:14:15.410
Man, that was brutal.

00:14:18.020 --> 00:14:20.540
Is Suzuki Aika-san...

00:14:20.890 --> 00:14:22.140
She's back.

00:14:22.140 --> 00:14:23.540
Really?

00:14:26.800 --> 00:14:30.180
I-I just got back.

00:14:32.160 --> 00:14:36.760
I don't care where you go or who 
you go with on your Saturdays.

00:14:36.760 --> 00:14:38.350
Not even if it's Suzuki-san.

00:14:38.350 --> 00:14:40.560
We didn't go out together.

00:14:40.560 --> 00:14:41.190
But!

00:14:41.570 --> 00:14:45.300
It's a different story if you're skipping
after party meetings to do it.

00:14:45.300 --> 00:14:46.690
And you didn't answer your phone.

00:14:47.240 --> 00:14:49.630
I-I forgot to take my phone with me.

00:14:49.630 --> 00:14:50.700
No excuses!

00:14:50.700 --> 00:14:52.140
Y-Yes, ma'am...

00:14:52.520 --> 00:14:56.130
Anyway, I think Suzuki-san is involved 
in the disappearances after—

00:14:56.130 --> 00:14:57.590
Don't change the subject.

00:14:58.000 --> 00:14:58.960
Sorry.

00:14:59.410 --> 00:15:02.800
I don't know whether to feel
jealous or sorry for him.

00:15:06.720 --> 00:15:08.170
I haven't seen her.

00:15:09.940 --> 00:15:10.930
What about you?

00:15:10.930 --> 00:15:12.300
I don't know.

00:15:12.820 --> 00:15:14.220
I see.

00:15:15.250 --> 00:15:17.760
Where could Suzuki-san be?

00:15:17.760 --> 00:15:18.690
Itsuki.

00:15:19.420 --> 00:15:21.600
Thanks for lunch.

00:15:21.600 --> 00:15:22.560
Sure.

00:15:22.560 --> 00:15:25.110
What? Silver, you ran into Itsuki-kun?

00:15:25.530 --> 00:15:26.860
While he was on his date.

00:15:27.790 --> 00:15:29.360
I see.

00:15:29.690 --> 00:15:31.740
E-Excuse me.

00:15:33.940 --> 00:15:34.820
Itsuki.

00:15:35.800 --> 00:15:37.870
I saw the ARKS you were talking about.

00:15:38.220 --> 00:15:40.060
Really? Where?

00:15:47.250 --> 00:15:48.700
Kill!

00:16:04.260 --> 00:16:05.520
I'll help.

00:16:06.440 --> 00:16:07.400
That's not necessary.

00:16:38.080 --> 00:16:41.430
Fomelgion!

00:16:54.870 --> 00:16:56.050
Wow.

00:16:58.780 --> 00:17:00.040
I failed to finish it off.

00:17:00.040 --> 00:17:01.160
Leave it to me!

00:17:05.390 --> 00:17:06.710
Don't, Itsuki!

00:17:18.940 --> 00:17:20.010
<i>Not good.</i>

00:17:26.200 --> 00:17:27.270
Itsuki!

00:17:56.230 --> 00:17:58.800
That's Over End...

00:18:24.440 --> 00:18:25.330
Are you okay?

00:18:25.330 --> 00:18:28.830
Suzuki-san, who in the world are you?

00:18:28.830 --> 00:18:29.800
What do you—

00:18:29.800 --> 00:18:30.960
Tell me.

00:18:32.700 --> 00:18:33.840
A guardian.

00:18:33.840 --> 00:18:36.710
A guardian? Of what?

00:18:36.710 --> 00:18:39.340
Itsuki, you still haven't noticed 
your own appearance?

00:18:41.360 --> 00:18:42.890
Wh-What is this?

00:18:42.890 --> 00:18:44.600
Why have I changed?

00:18:44.970 --> 00:18:46.260
You'll learn eventually.

00:18:47.120 --> 00:18:49.600
Hey, wait. I'm not done talking.

00:18:54.200 --> 00:18:57.610
They seem to have noticed, as well.

00:18:58.220 --> 00:18:59.640
You know what this means.

00:18:59.640 --> 00:19:00.650
Roger that.

00:19:01.000 --> 00:19:03.120
I'm off to eliminate more Darkers.

00:19:13.790 --> 00:19:14.790
<b>Girls' Dorm Ahead</b>

00:19:13.790 --> 00:19:14.790
<b>No Boys Allowed!!</b>

00:19:16.160 --> 00:19:17.260
Hold it!

00:19:21.630 --> 00:19:23.680
<b>Sakura Candy Drops</b>

00:19:24.440 --> 00:19:25.580
I'm good.

00:19:30.900 --> 00:19:34.690
I remember doing something similar
in my high school days, too.

00:19:34.690 --> 00:19:38.000
I had girls on my mind 
and acted without thinking.

00:19:38.000 --> 00:19:40.830
It's part of being young.

00:19:40.830 --> 00:19:44.520
But you still have to follow the rules.

00:19:41.660 --> 00:19:43.720
Is Ai-Ai in one of the free rooms?

00:19:43.720 --> 00:19:44.520
No.

00:19:45.520 --> 00:19:49.260
Even I broke a rule or two, but...

00:19:49.700 --> 00:19:51.930
What are we going to do?

00:19:51.930 --> 00:19:53.710
Suzuki-san's not in her room?

00:19:54.280 --> 00:19:58.210
No. We were going to talk to her 
about her maid café uniform.

00:19:58.650 --> 00:20:01.620
Hey, I'm still talking here!

00:20:04.500 --> 00:20:05.780
What's wrong?

00:20:05.780 --> 00:20:08.060
Nothing. Sorry to have bothered you.

00:20:08.470 --> 00:20:09.570
Hey!

00:20:09.910 --> 00:20:12.980
I was just getting to the 
really bittersweet man talk!

00:20:22.980 --> 00:20:24.020
Why?

00:20:40.660 --> 00:20:42.180
Wh-What is that?

00:20:42.510 --> 00:20:43.760
Are you kidding me?!

00:20:57.520 --> 00:20:59.160
Suzuki-san?

00:21:00.470 --> 00:21:01.690
What is this?

00:21:01.960 --> 00:21:03.110
What's going on?

00:21:09.030 --> 00:21:09.810
Run.

00:21:09.810 --> 00:21:10.410
What?

00:21:10.410 --> 00:21:11.440
Go! Now!

00:21:31.830 --> 00:21:32.430
What?

00:21:38.810 --> 00:21:40.190
So he's awakened.

00:23:39.520 --> 00:23:41.070
<b>Next Episode</b>

00:23:41.070 --> 00:24:08.960
<b>Next Episode</b>

00:23:42.010 --> 00:23:43.100
Hey.

00:23:43.100 --> 00:23:44.910
Don't you think we lack presence?

00:23:44.910 --> 00:23:46.560
Yeah, we're pretty plain.

00:23:46.810 --> 00:23:48.720
Is there any opportunity for us to stand out?

00:23:48.720 --> 00:23:50.140
Don't copy me.

00:23:50.140 --> 00:23:51.260
No you.

00:23:51.550 --> 00:23:53.840
Starting next week, we're getting 
ready for the school festival.

00:23:53.840 --> 00:23:56.750
I'm sure we'll get our chance to shine, too.

00:23:56.750 --> 00:23:58.180
Try not to steal the spotlight.

00:23:58.450 --> 00:23:59.740
You copied me again.

00:23:59.740 --> 00:24:01.570
No, you copied me.

00:24:01.570 --> 00:24:03.000
If you're that desperate for attention,

00:24:03.000 --> 00:24:05.890
maybe you should keep 
talking at the same time.

00:24:06.190 --> 00:24:07.310
That's it!
